    <h1>A Touch of Vanilla to Your Nitro Coffee</h1>
    <p class="muted">By John Goerke. <time datetime="2020-10-06">October 6, 2020</time>.</p>

    <p>Coffee is versatile, and flavor is one of the easiest ways to make it your own. This article looks at adding a touch of vanilla to nitro coffee.</p>

    <h2>Why vanilla works with nitro cold brew</h2>
    <p><a href="/nitro-cold-brew/">Nitro cold brew</a> is naturally sweet and finishes smooth. Vanilla complements both, so a little goes a long way and the coffee stays the star.</p>

    <h2>Flavored nitro coffee</h2>
    <p>Flavored nitro coffee is one example of how flexible coffee on tap can be. Learn more about <a href="/nitro-coffee-kegs/">nitro coffee kegs</a> or see the <a href="/kegerators/">equipment to serve nitro on tap</a>.</p>

    <p>Questions about flavors? <a href="/contact-bona-fide-nitro-coffee-and-tea/">Contact us</a>.</p>
